## AI-Assisted

## Capture helper for the derivative-maker variable snapshots. Run with the current
## directory ALREADY inside the derivative-maker checkout: sources the required
## help-steps/pre bootstrap, then runs the capture command passed as arguments:
##   - 'declare -p' / 'declare -F'                       (the bare-pre baseline), or
##   - 'source help-steps/variables <build-args>'        (a full build-command capture;
##     the dist_build_dump_varnames / dist_build_dump_funcnames env hook prints the dump).
##
## Split out of an inline 'bash -c "source ...; source ..."' so each capture is a single
## command invocation, not a multi-statement inline '-c' (R-192). The caller supplies the
## deterministic env (dist_build_* pins) via 'env ...' before this script.
## style-ok: no-strict -- the sourced help-steps/pre + variables manage their own strict mode;
## adding it here would change what the snapshot captures.

## help-steps/pre is in the derivative-maker checkout (the current directory at call time),
## not resolvable from this file's location.
# shellcheck disable=SC1091
source help-steps/pre
"$@"
